hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16831","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to me from Yahya ibn Umara from his grandfather Abu Hasan, he said: I entered the markets, and he said: And I picked, and al-Qawariri once said: And I took two unripe dates, he said: And their mother was sprinkling over them while I wanted to take them, he said: And Abu Hasan came upon me and pulled out a palm stalk, he said: And he struck me with it, and a woman of ours called Maryam said to me: You have been wretched from his upper arm and from the breaking of the palm stalk. And he said to me: Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made forbidden what is between the two lava tracts of Medina?"
